    "source": "substack",
    "posted": "2025-11-10",
    "asset_hint": "BTC",
    "timeframe_hint": "1d",
    "category": "rule",
    "excerpt": "A bullish trade is generated whenever the current short-term SMA is above the current long-term SMA and the previous RSI is below the oversold level and below the current RSI. \u2026 We will tweak the following parameters and back-test on the daily values of BTCUSD: \u2026 short_len = 200, long_len = 300, rsi_ov = 65, rsi_us = 35, initial_capital = 100000, holding_period = 20 \u2026 holding_period = this is the number of periods to hold before liquidating \u2026 The results were... surprising.",
    "performance_claim": null,
    "verbatim_confidence": "high",
    "notes": "SMA 200/300 trend filter + RSI 35 hook, 20-bar hold, BTC daily 2019-2025; parameter lines were code-formatted on page (backticks dropped), results only in images."
  },
